WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.449
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.550
Our relentless stampede
towards wealth and comfort

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.710
has cracked open our Earth.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.560
Can you feel her,
sagging and groaning

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.910
under the weight of our greed,
ecosystems severed, barren,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:19.750
and bleeding?

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.710
But all hail progress, right?

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.430
We have bruised, and abused,
and depleted our lands.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.880
Given warning after
warning, we bide our time.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.080
Knowledge is no longer the
great barrier it once was.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.070
Earth is shedding
her familiar skin,

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.280
and this home will
no longer welcome

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.510
we, who have squandered
our humanity on progress.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:49.425
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.910
We no longer have the luxury
of tending to our own,

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.180
waiting for someone
somewhere to do something,

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.470
gorging on articles,
reports, statements, acting

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.020
as if taking in more information
will change in our fate.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.920
The truth is laid out in broad,
scorching daylight, written

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.980
in oil, and blood,
and ash, cosigned

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.572
by the cries of ancient wisdom.

00:05:46.572 --> 00:05:48.460
We did this.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:51.812
We've run out of time, and
consequence is not on our side.

00:05:51.812 --> 00:05:54.788
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.900
But before you drown in
this sea of pointed fingers,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.620
before you aim your fists
in blame, lift up your hand

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.130
and say, yes, to the future
that is now ours to construct.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:19.660
Despair is not an option.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:23.090
Our ancestors have not survived
the catastrophes the war,

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.330
famine, and enslavement just so
that our fragile spines could

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.215
not even break the
glass on our screens.

00:06:29.215 --> 00:06:31.598
Stop screaming into
your boxes, and look up!

00:06:31.598 --> 00:06:34.592
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.670
We must press forward.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:33.820
Hope is the only option is
hope is the only option is hope

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.460
is the only option is hope is--

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.110
the only option
is to not opt-out.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.700
We will not opt-out.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.690
We will not be enslaved
by our desire for power,

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:48.520
our desperation for power,
our dependence on power.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.910
But can we regenerate
this world with our power,

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.960
our wealth, our knowledge?

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:56.200
Our know holds the
power to change.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.020
We can't just stop
this train of progress.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.460
We must reroute.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.375
We must heal the damage.

00:08:02.375 --> 00:08:02.875
We must--

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.260
But the one thing we need
more than hope is action.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:35.040
Once we start to act,
hope is everywhere.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.790
So instead of looking for
hope, look for action.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.700
Then and only then,
hope will come.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.750
[APPLAUSE]

